Clearly, learning the cmavo is far easier than
learning the cmavo + all the vocabulary.

> > 1) Loglish is much easier to train users in
> > than Lojban
>
> Yes, because of the vocabulary learning.  The
> rest would be on a par, with the cmavo learning a
> bit harder perhaps. I don't know how significant
> the difference would be.

IMO, for an individual with some background in
logic and a high IQ -- but without a photographic
memory -- learning the vocabulary will be
by far the most time-consuming part of learning
Lojban.

For an individual with lower IQ and no background
in logic, the formulation of thoughts in predicate
logic may be difficult and unnatural, and may form
the largest obstacle to learning Lojban.  I don't
know if anyone has any experience with this -- so
far as I know, everyone who's bothered to learn a
significant amount of Lojban is pretty clever and
with an explicitly rationalist mindest.

